---
// The landing page. Sections + copy match the systeme.io original Pascal
// supplied; rebuilding it in Astro brings: AEO-grade JSON-LD, scroll-reveal,
// Astro <Image> optimization (sharp generates WebP variants at build), and
// PostHog hooks via data-ph-capture-attribute-cta on every download CTA.

import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DownloadButtons from '~/components/DownloadButtons.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import founderImage from '~/assets/founder.png';
import { SITE } from '~/consts';
import { absoluteUrl } from '~/lib/url';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={SITE.title}
  description={SITE.description}
  canonicalURL={absoluteUrl('/')}
>
  <section class="hero container" id="top">
    <div class="hero__label" data-reveal>Quarter · Week · Today — in one app</div>
    <h1 data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 80ms">
      Your big goals and today's tasks.<br />One app. <em>No switching.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="hero__sub" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 160ms">
      You set a quarterly goal in Notion. Your todo list lives in Apple Reminders. Your calendar forgets the why. Focus Mode One is the one place where your 90&#8209;day vision and today's next 90 minutes are wired together — so you actually ship what matters.
    </p>
    <div class="hero__cta" id="download" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 240ms">
      <DownloadButtons location="hero" variant="hero" />
      <p class="hero__legal">7&#8209;day free trial on any tier. Cancel anytime in App Store settings.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pain">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow" data-reveal>The problem you keep living with</span>
      <h2 data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 80ms">
        You don't need another app. You need <em>connection</em>.
      </h2>
      <p class="pain__lede" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 160ms">
        The average productivity person uses five tools. And re-builds the link between their vision and their day every single Monday. The link is the bottleneck.
      </p>
      <div class="pain__grid">
        <div class="pain-card" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 240ms">
          <div class="pain-card__num">01</div>
          <h3>Goals die in a separate app</h3>
          <p>Your quarter plan lives in a doc you opened once in January. By March, it's a graveyard.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pain-card" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 320ms">
          <div class="pain-card__num">02</div>
          <h3>Today's tasks have no why</h3>
          <p>Your todo list is full. But nothing on it moves your actual goals forward. You finish the day tired and unclear.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pain-card" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 400ms">
          <div class="pain-card__num">03</div>
          <h3>Sunday planning is a chore</h3>
          <p>You spend an hour every weekend rebuilding the bridge between vision and week. Then ignore it by Wednesday.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="dimensions container" id="dimensions">
    <span class="eyebrow" data-reveal>The solution</span>
    <h2 data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 80ms">
      Three dimensions. One view.<br />Every day.
    </h2>
    <p class="dimensions__lede" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 160ms">
      Focus Mode One is built around one idea: your quarter, your week, and your day should live in the same place — and talk to each other.
    </p>
    <div class="dim-grid">
      <div class="dim-card dim-card--athena" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 240ms">
        <div class="dim-card__label">Quarter</div>
        <h3>The arrow.</h3>
        <span class="dim-card__limit">Max 3 goals</span>
        <p>
          What matters in the next 90 days. A guided Focus Future ritual turns a blank page into three concrete outcomes you actually commit to.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="dim-card dim-card--hermes" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 320ms">
        <div class="dim-card__label">Week</div>
        <h3>The bridge.</h3>
        <span class="dim-card__limit">3 ideally · max 6</span>
        <p>
          What actually ships this week. A weekly planning wizard pulls from your quarter — so the link is built for you, not by you.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="dim-card dim-card--eos" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 400ms">
        <div class="dim-card__label">Today</div>
        <h3>The execution.</h3>
        <span class="dim-card__limit">3 big · 6 supporting</span>
        <p>
          What you do in the next eight hours. Each day task links back to its week goal, which links to its quarter goal. No orphans.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="rule">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="rule__layout">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow" data-reveal>The rule of three</span>
          <h2 data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 80ms">
            Less, by design.<br />That's what focus <em>is</em>.
          </h2>
          <p data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 160ms">
            Most productivity apps let you drown in endless tasks. Focus Mode One enforces limits — because focus isn't deciding what to do. It's deciding what <strong style="color:#F0EFE8">not</strong> to do.
          </p>
          <p data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 240ms">
            Hit the cap and the app won't let you add more. Painful at first. Then liberating.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rule__stats">
          <div class="stat stat--athena" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 160ms">
            <div class="stat__num">3</div>
            <div class="stat__text">quarterly goals. <strong>Three is the hard cap</strong> — no overflow. Focus Future wizard guides you to the right three.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="stat stat--hermes" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 240ms">
            <div class="stat__num">3</div>
            <div class="stat__text">weekly goals, ideally. <strong>Max 6</strong> if the week demands it. Pulled forward from the quarter via Weekly Launch Pad.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="stat stat--eos" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 320ms">
            <div class="stat__num">9</div>
            <div class="stat__text">daily slots max. <strong>3 priorities + 6 supporting</strong>. Or a 1/3/5 mix if that's your rhythm. Every slot traces back to a bigger goal.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="features container" id="features">
    <span class="eyebrow" style="display:block;text-align:center" data-reveal>What's inside</span>
    <h2 data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 80ms">One app. Every ritual.</h2>
    <p class="features__lede" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 160ms">
      Built for deep work, not shallow busywork. Every feature exists because it helps you connect vision to execution.
    </p>
    <div class="feat-grid">

      <div class="feat feat--eos" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 40ms">
        <div class="feat__icon">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" /><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Focus Mode sessions</h3>
        <p>Slide to start a full-screen timer. No notifications, no taps out. If the app crashes mid-session it picks right back up. Extend on the fly when you're in flow.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="feat" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 80ms">
        <div class="feat__icon">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M9 11l3 3L22 4" /><path d="M21 12v7a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h11" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Goal linking that sticks</h3>
        <p>Every day task can be linked to a week goal. Every week goal can be linked to a quarterly KR. Counter-based KRs even roll up automatically — knock out a day task, the quarterly number moves.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="feat feat--hermes" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 120ms">
        <div class="feat__icon">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M13 2L3 14h9l-1 8 10-12h-9l1-8z" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Guided planning wizards</h3>
        <p>Weekly Launch Pad and Focus Future walk you through planning instead of staring at a blank page. You answer five questions; the app sets up your week or quarter.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="feat" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 160ms">
        <div class="feat__icon">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M6 9H4.5a2.5 2.5 0 0 1 0-5H6" /><path d="M18 9h1.5a2.5 2.5 0 0 0 0-5H18" />
            <path d="M4 22h16" /><path d="M10 14.66V17c0 .55-.47.98-.97 1.21C7.85 18.75 7 20.24 7 22" />
            <path d="M14 14.66V17c0 .55.47.98.97 1.21C16.15 18.75 17 20.24 17 22" /><path d="M18 2H6v7a6 6 0 0 0 12 0V2z" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Streaks, trophies, XP</h3>
        <p>18 trophies across day, week, and quarter wins. Earn XP per task. Rank up from Focused to Legendary. A light-touch gamification layer that respects your attention.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="feat feat--eos" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 200ms">
        <div class="feat__icon">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M12 2a10 10 0 1 0 10 10" /><path d="M12 6v6l4 2" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>The Anchor</h3>
        <p>One sentence you wrote that you see every morning — your mindset, your why, whatever keeps you steady. Optional daily notification at the time you choose.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="feat" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 240ms">
        <div class="feat__icon">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="18" rx="2" /><line x1="16" y1="2" x2="16" y2="6" />
            <line x1="8" y1="2" x2="8" y2="6" /><line x1="3" y1="10" x2="21" y2="10" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Weekly Promise Tracker</h3>
        <p>A visual record of every week you kept your promise to yourself. Weeks under 80% crack. Weeks over 80% shine. Over months, it tells you the truth about your consistency.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="feat feat--hermes" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 280ms">
        <div class="feat__icon">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M19 21l-7-5-7 5V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h10a2 2 0 0 1 2 2z" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Someday Shelf</h3>
        <p>Ideas you don't want to lose, but can't do this week. A single bookmarked shelf. Revisit on your next planning day — restore with one tap.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="feat" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 320ms">
        <div class="feat__icon">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M12 2v20" /><path d="M17 5H9.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 0 0 7h5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7H6" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Cross-device sync</h3>
        <p>Backed by Supabase (EU region). Your data syncs instantly across iPhone and iPad. Sign in with Apple, Google, or email.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="feat feat--eos" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 360ms">
        <div class="feat__icon">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M21 11.5a8.38 8.38 0 0 1-.9 3.8 8.5 8.5 0 0 1-7.6 4.7 8.38 8.38 0 0 1-3.8-.9L3 21l1.9-5.7a8.38 8.38 0 0 1-.9-3.8 8.5 8.5 0 0 1 4.7-7.6 8.38 8.38 0 0 1 3.8-.9h.5a8.48 8.48 0 0 1 8 8v.5z" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>iOS-native polish</h3>
        <p>Thoughtful haptics on every completion. Smooth dark-mode design. Built to feel like Apple ships it — because that's how focus tools should feel.</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="founder" id="founder">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="founder__layout">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Why I built this</span>
          <h2 data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 80ms">
            I was switching <em>five apps</em> before breakfast.
          </h2>
          <p data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 160ms">
            Notion held my quarterly goals. Apple Reminders held today. My calendar knew the time but not the meaning. My notes app had last week's reflection in a file I'd never open again.
          </p>
          <p data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 240ms">
            Every Monday I spent an hour re-building the bridge between my big vision and the next five days. By Thursday, the bridge was gone again. I wasn't lacking discipline. I was lacking a single place where these three dimensions — quarter, week, today — were wired together by default.
          </p>
          <p data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 320ms">
            Focus Mode One is the tool I wished existed. It enforces the constraints that actually produce focus (three goals, not thirty), it builds the link between 90 days and 90 minutes for you, and it gets out of your way during the one hour that matters: when you're doing the work.
          </p>
          <p class="founder__sig" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 400ms">
            — Pascal
            <small>Founder · Focus Mode One</small>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="founder__image" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 160ms">
          <Image
            src={founderImage}
            alt="Pascal Weihrauch, founder of Focus Mode One"
            widths={[340, 680, 1020]}
            sizes="(max-width: 860px) 80vw, 340px"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="final-cta">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--athena" data-reveal>Your next 90 days</span>
      <h2 data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 80ms">
        Start shipping what <em>actually</em> matters.
      </h2>
      <p data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 160ms">
        Download Focus Mode One, run the Focus Future wizard in 10 minutes, and finish this week with three goals that connect directly to your quarter. 7&#8209;day free trial. No credit card required at sign-up.
      </p>
      <div data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 240ms">
        <DownloadButtons location="final" variant="final" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
